OL,3,CLatest hosepipe ban comes into force
OL,4,Cas forecasters warn of flooding
OL,6,FBy Friday, the conditions are expected
OL,7,Fto turn drier once again through the
OL,8,Fweekend before more rain is forecast
OL,9,Fnext week.
OL,11,FThe change comes after the UK's fifth
OL,12,Fheatwave of the summer, during which
OL,13,Fthe hottest day of the year was
OL,14,Frecorded in Kew Gardens, London, on
OL,15,FThursday when temperatures reached
OL,16,F38.1C.
OL,18,FThe forecast rain may bring some
OL,19,Fwelcome relief to parched land and
OL,20,Ffire-fighters tackling wildfires.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30406
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1787015895
OL,3,CLatest hosepipe ban comes into force
OL,4,Cas forecasters warn of flooding
OL,6,FBut it is unlikely to bring an end to
OL,7,Fwidespread drought conditions that
OL,8,Fhave put severe pressure on wildlife,
OL,9,Ffarmers, transport, emergency services
OL,10,Finfrastructure and water resources.
OL,12,FAmong the driest areas in the UK are
OL,13,FWisley in Surrey, which has recorded
OL,14,F61 consecutive dry days since June 17,
OL,15,Fand Heathrow in Greater London, which
OL,16,Fhas measured 55 consecutive dry days
OL,17,Fsince June 23, according to Met Office
OL,18,Fdata.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/8
